From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_AHEAD_LOAD_WAIT=1: a frame ahead, a present waits for its own frame around a fade to black, a load or a stall; off by default

Door walk, cut to Link's house, all runs checked so far (check.py): with the full wait the cut is
clean in 45 of 45 runs. A frame ahead (EDEN_NX2_FRAMES_AHEAD=1) it is over-bright in 8 of 20 runs
without a guard and in 4 of 12 with EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD=3; in 3 of 3 with the guard's front notes
and 3 of 3 with EDEN_UP_UBO_AHEAD, the two that take a frame's constant buffers early. It is not
one frame: whole-picture brightness per game frame after the black runs 9, 91, 81, 74, 72, 62 ...
47 over about a second, against 9, 18, 33, 40, 43, 45 in a clean run. So the first frame is the
same, the second has the exposure far too high, and it then comes down at the slow rate: the
exposure was set from a wrong reading right after the cut.

The reading this points to, not shown directly: the exposure meter, a sum the GPU writes and the
game reads and clears every frame (the 'read the sum, then store 0' of EDEN_NX2_OVERWRITE_CHECK).
Its download lands at the frame's fence, and a frame ahead the game reads before that.

EDEN_UP_OOT_LOAD_WAIT already has the test for 'not steady gameplay' (under 300 draws twice in a
row, or presents more than 250 ms apart) but does nothing with EDEN_NX2_FRAMES_AHEAD=1. This
switch applies the same test there: while unsteady, and for EDEN_UP_OOT_LOAD_WAIT_HOLD_MS after
(700 ms by default with this switch alone), the present also waits for its own frame, as it
already does when the GPU is behind. Steady gameplay is untouched.

diff --git a/src/common/nx2_load_wait.h b/src/common/nx2_load_wait.h
index edff555..c4a5c5c 100644
--- a/src/common/nx2_load_wait.h
+++ b/src/common/nx2_load_wait.h
@@ -42,12 +42,33 @@ namespace Common::Nx2LoadWait {
     return enabled;
 }
 
+/// EDEN_UP_AHEAD_LOAD_WAIT=1 (exact "1", Ocarina of Time only, with EDEN_NX2_FRAMES_AHEAD=1, where
+/// EDEN_UP_OOT_LOAD_WAIT does nothing): the same test decides, present by present, whether a
+/// present that would return a frame ahead waits for its own frame instead. The hold after the
+/// last unsteady present is 700 ms by default here (EDEN_UP_OOT_LOAD_WAIT_HOLD_MS sets it).
+///
+/// Why: T91-T97, door walk, cut to Link's house: in 12 of 32 runs a frame ahead (with or
+/// without EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD) the second frame after the black came out at about twice the
+/// brightness and took a second to settle (whole-picture brightness 9, 91, 81, 74 ... 47 against
+/// 9, 18, 33, 40, 43, 45), in 0 of 45 runs with the full wait. That is the exposure set from a
+/// wrong reading and then adapting at its slow rate. The reading it points to (not shown
+/// directly): the game's exposure meter, a sum the GPU writes and the game reads and clears each
+/// frame; a frame ahead the game reads it before the frame in flight has written it. In steady
+/// gameplay the exposure moves slowly and a frame of lag shows nothing; right after a cut the
+/// game sets it from one reading. The black before a cut draws next to nothing, so it is
+/// unsteady by the test above, and the hold carries the full wait over the first frames of the
+/// new scene.
+[[nodiscard]] inline bool AheadEnabled() {
+    static const bool enabled = PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_AHEAD_LOAD_WAIT");
+    return enabled;
+}
+
 /// 3D draws run since the last present took the count. Any thread.
 inline std::atomic<u64> g_draws{};
 
 /// The thread that runs the 3D engine, for each draw it runs.
 inline void NoteDraw() {
-    if (Enabled()) {
+    if (Enabled() || AheadEnabled()) {
         g_draws.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed);
     }
 }
@@ -70,7 +91,8 @@ inline void NoteDraw() {
     static const auto slow =
         std::chrono::milliseconds{Setting("EDEN_UP_OOT_LOAD_WAIT_SLOW_MS", 250, 1, 60'000)};
     static const auto hold =
-        std::chrono::milliseconds{Setting("EDEN_UP_OOT_LOAD_WAIT_HOLD_MS", 8000, 0, 600'000)};
+        std::chrono::milliseconds{Setting("EDEN_UP_OOT_LOAD_WAIT_HOLD_MS",
+                                          AheadEnabled() && !Enabled() ? 700 : 8000, 0, 600'000)};
     static Clock::time_point last_present = Clock::now();
     static Clock::time_point last_unsteady = last_present;
     static bool steady = false;
@@ -94,9 +116,10 @@ inline void NoteDraw() {
     const bool now_steady = now - last_unsteady >= hold;
     if (presents == 0) {
         LOG_INFO(Service,
-                 "EDEN_UP_OOT_LOAD_WAIT=1: full frame wait until every present has run at least "
+                 "{}=1: full frame wait until every present has run at least "
                  "{} draws and come within {} ms of the one before for {} ms",
-                 min_draws, slow.count(), hold.count());
+                 Enabled() ? "EDEN_UP_OOT_LOAD_WAIT" : "EDEN_UP_AHEAD_LOAD_WAIT", min_draws,
+                 slow.count(), hold.count());
     }
     if (now_steady != steady) {
         steady = now_steady;
